  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Program Continuation Grant for Scaling Up Malaria Control Interventions Towards Universal Coverage in Sierra Leone - Sierra Leone (01-Jul-2018-30-Jun-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sierra Leone, Malaria, Catholic Relief Services - United States Conference of Catholic Bishops (CRS Sierra Leone)This program has the following goals: By 2020, reduce malaria morbidity and mortality by at least 40% compared with 2015.. The objectives of this program are: All suspected malaria cases should have access to confirmatory diagnosis.  All malaria cases to receive effective treatment..  Provide access to 100% of the population at risk with preventive measures by 2017.  To protect at least 80 % of pregnant women and children under one year with IPT 3 by 2020.  To provide knowledge to the population such that at least 80% practise malaria prevention and treatment measures by 2018..  By 2020, at least 95% of health facilities report routinely on malaria programme performance..  By 2020, maintain and strengthen capacity for program management, coordination and partnership to achieve malaria programme performance at all levels.</narrative>
  </description>
